#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""vpnctl — manage VPN servers on this host for the panel: AmneziaWG, SSTP (accel-ppp), VLESS (Xray REALITY),
and Telegram proxies (MTProto over fake TLS): telemt and mtg.

The panel calls it locally (sudo) or over SSH (forced command, see --ssh). Output: JSON on the last line.

  vpnctl list | dump [UNIT ...] | params UNIT | next-ip UNIT
  vpnctl add UNIT --pub ID [--ip IP] [--name NAME]     # secret on stdin: AWG preshared key / SSTP password /
                                                       # telemt user secret (32 hex)
  vpnctl remove|disable|enable UNIT --pub ID
  vpnctl set-name UNIT --pub ID --name NAME
  vpnctl install awg3|sstp|vless|telemt|mtg [--port N] [--sni HOST] [--domain NAME]
                                                       # telemt/mtg: --sni is the site the proxy pretends to be
  vpnctl uninstall awg3|sstp|vless|telemt|mtg          # container removed, data kept aside
  vpnctl preflight | unlink | version

Units and identities (ID):
  awg3, amnezia-awg2, amnezia-awg, amnezia-wireguard   AmneziaWG public key
  sstp (container), sstp-host (system accel-ppp)       login
  xray                                                 VLESS uuid
  telemt                                               user name (each user has its own secret)
  mtg-doppel                                           always "shared": mtg has one secret for everybody

Secrets never leave the host: private/preshared keys, passwords and telemt user secrets are not printed.
The one exception is `params mtg-doppel`: mtg has a single shared secret, and that secret IS the proxy link
the panel has to hand out, so it is returned there (and only there).
"""
